{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27146335","formula":"C₅H₅N₃O₃","hill":"C5H5N3O3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":5.0,"H":5.0,"N":3.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Cytosine-5-carboxylic acid"},"descriptions":{"en":"5-Carboxylcytosine (5caC) is a modified nucleobase, derived from cytosine, that plays a significant role as an intermediate in the process of active DNA demethylation. It is generated through the oxidation of 5-methylcytosine (5mC) via 5-hydroxymethylcytosine (5hmC) and 5-formylcytosine (5fC), catalyzed by the TET family of dioxygenases. 5caC represents the final oxidative state in this pathway before the base is typically removed and replaced with an unmodified cytosine by Terminal deoxynucleotidyl transferase (TdT) or Thymine DNA glycosylase (TDG) by base excision repair."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":77213,"mass":155.11,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=NC(=O)NC(=C1C(=O)O)N","inchikey":"BLQMCTXZEMGOJM-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"6-amino-2-oxo-1H-pyrimidine-5-carboxylic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"77213","atoms":16,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.445,"y":-1.492,"z":0.482,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.394,"y":-0.04,"z":-0.005,"el":"O"},{"x":2.867,"y":0.542,"z":-0.474,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.378,"y":1.011,"z":0.084,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.525,"y":-1.347,"z":-0.132,"el":"N"},{"x":0.637,"y":2.236,"z":0.191,"el":"N"},{"x":0.006,"y":1.025,"z":0.082,"el":"C"},{"x":0.64,"y":-0.159,"z":-0.029,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.234,"y":-1.349,"z":-0.135,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.166,"y":-0.13,"z":-0.018,"el":"C"},{"x":2.101,"y":-0.299,"z":-0.046,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.843,"y":1.91,"z":0.168,"el":"H"},{"x":0.274,"y":-2.321,"z":-0.241,"el":"H"},{"x":1.647,"y":2.292,"z":0.195,"el":"H"},{"x":0.079,"y":3.077,"z":0.27,"el":"H"},{"x":3.417,"y":-1.625,"z":0.489,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,10,1],[0,15,1],[1,9,2],[2